From da181c86bdafb3dead4036a8d9b791f6e75990c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 06:54:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] system: Submit Log keeps the log on the system, filtered,
 unless its upload is chosen

The two buttons under "Submit Log" sent what pastekodi or pastecrash
collect to the paste service of LibreELEC (paste.libreelec.tv) as soon
as they were pressed, under what LibreELEC's script says of itself. This
is not LibreELEC's build, and its other texts say that Team LibreELEC
does not support it: a log should not leave for LibreELEC's service
without the user having chosen that. And such a log is not harmless: the
log of the media centre and the journal go into it as they are, with the
addresses that add-ons open, which can carry the keys of the services
that they use.

Each button now asks where the log goes.

- "Keep it on this system", which comes first and has the focus. The
  command is told to print (-c, the option that pastekodi has for it),
  and what it prints goes through the filter of the diagnostics
  (/usr/lib/hades-diag/redact.sed, called as they call it: addresses are
  cut down to their server, what it takes for a key or a password is
  taken out, and a line that is too long for it is left out) into
  /storage/logfiles/system-log-<date>-<time>.txt
  (crash-log-... for the crash log), the folder that LibreELEC has for
  logs and shares as "Logfiles". What the filter prints is copied to the
  file by the add-on, which does not look at it: a write that fails is
  then an error of the add-on, where sed says nothing of one in the last
  that it writes. The file gets its name when the command and the filter
  have ended well and what the filter printed is on the drive, and the
  name is written through after it; it is whatever the command wrote,
  which is no more complete than an upload would be. A command or a
  filter that fails, prints nothing, cannot be run, or is not done two
  minutes after the start (both are stopped then, the command with what
  it started) leaves no file; nothing unfiltered is ever kept in the
  place of a filtered log; and unfinished files that an earlier run left
  behind (a power cut) are taken away. A name that is taken (a clock that
  went back) is not taken again: the log gets a number after it. Then the
  add-on says where the file is, that nothing was sent, what the filter
  does and that no filter knows everything, and how to take the file
  away; where the storage is in memory, as in live mode, also that the
  log is gone when the system is turned off.
- "Upload it to the paste service of LibreELEC": what the buttons did,
  after a text that says where the log goes, as it is; that whoever has
  its address can read it there; that it can hold keys and passwords, and
  that an upload is not filtered; and that Team LibreELEC does not
  support this build. Then a question with "No" preselected, and nothing
  is uploaded while Kodi is stopping (Kodi answers a question that it
  does not show then with the answer that the last one got).

Leaving the first question without an answer does nothing. No entry of it
is preselected, because Kodi answers with a preselected entry when
something else closes the dialog.

One thing changes in the upload itself: what became of it is said also
when Cancel was pressed while it went on. Cancel stops nothing there, and
LibreELEC's code then said nothing of a log that was sent all the same.

The labels and the help of the two buttons are new texts, in English and
in Spanish (the help that LibreELEC has for them still names ix.io, where
its script no longer sends anything). The texts that they replace stay in
the files as they are. The commands paste, pastekodi and pastecrash are
not touched by this patch.
